00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.389 align:start position:0%
these ukrainians boarding a ferry to  cross into romania are facing a future  they never imagined  many have been living in bombed out  towns in the freezing cold without heat  light and water  now they hope they'll be safe  but the fighting is preventing many from  reaching safety through humanitarian  corridors  ukrainian president vladimir zelinsky  says russian forces are targeting  civilians despite promises of a  ceasefire in several areas of the  country  president vladimir putin says the  ukrainians are sabotaging russia's  efforts to evacuate people  six humanitarian corridors have been  open from mariopol detailed information  about these routes were given well in  advance to the osce the red cross and to  the ukrainians russian forces will be  monitoring them 24 7.  in the capital kiev there is resolve  preparation  i'm carrying out my duty working for my  country thanking our soldiers that's why  i'm here and i'm very proud of it  and clarity about the violence to come  every house every street every  checkpoint we will fight to the death if  necessary no one wants to die but if  necessary we will protect most of all  our children our families  there is now a 65 kilometer long convoy  of russian tanks and armored vehicles  making a steady approach towards the  capital amid fierce ukrainian resistance  we do have indications that this  operation would be unsustainable within  about three weeks from the motion  perspective  in which case that they would have to  consolidate their gains already made  and look to see a way of trying to  freeze the conflict on the current lines  of advance  there are concerns whether a ceasefire  declared by russia can hold to allow  more civilians to escape  the u.n refugee agency says hundreds of  civilians have been killed  six health care workers have also died  according to the world health  organization but the number of deaths  are sure to rise  natasha name al jazeera
 

